WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.894
Swift continuations

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:02.826
hide the nastiest

00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:03.887
concurrency bugs

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:06.120
Most iOS codebases

00:00:06.155 --> 00:00:07.228
still have callback

00:00:07.111 --> 00:00:08.101
APIs at their

00:00:07.913 --> 00:00:08.478
edges

00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:10.247
an analytics SDK

00:00:10.413 --> 00:00:11.497
a Bluetooth stack

00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:12.818
a payment library

00:00:12.677 --> 00:00:13.572
or an old

00:00:13.384 --> 00:00:14.929
networking layer nobody

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:15.719
wants to rewrite

00:00:16.246 --> 00:00:17.684
Continuations are how

00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:18.769
those APIs become

00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:19.972
async functions

00:00:20.111 --> 00:00:21.254
The conversion looks

00:00:21.066 --> 00:00:21.762
trivial

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:22.552
but it is

00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:23.200
where the author

00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:23.743
has seen the

00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:24.957
most subtle concurrency

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:25.464
bugs

00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:26.807
The bugs are

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:27.727
tasks that hang

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:28.883
forever and sudden

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.472
crashes

00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:30.687
including the double

00:00:30.499 --> 00:00:31.572
resume problem

00:00:31.666 --> 00:00:32.586
which the article

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:33.612
fixes by taking

00:00:33.423 --> 00:00:34.744
the continuation under

00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:35.251
a lock

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:36.804
Full story on

00:00:36.615 --> 00:00:37.511
the dashboard
